# Disclosure allowlist - HybridHELIX Website 4.0
#
# Read by .github/scripts/disclosure-scan.sh. Each non-comment line is a literal
# string that is APPROVED FOR PUBLICATION. A finding whose matched text equals an
# entry here is suppressed.
#
# This file exists so that publishing something sensitive is a deliberate,
# reviewable act rather than an accident. Adding a line here is a decision. It
# shows up in a diff, it gets reviewed like any other change, and the reason is
# recorded next to it.
#
# Rules of use:
#   - One literal value per line. Not a regex. It must match the flagged text exactly.
#   - Always leave a comment saying who approved it and why.
#   - Do not add a value here to make a red build go green. Remove the value from
#     the page instead, unless it genuinely belongs on a public site.
#   - Credentials are never allowlisted. Rotate them.
#
# Format:
#   <literal value>   # approved by <who>, <date> - <why>
#
# Intentionally empty. Nothing has been pre-approved. The first entries should
# be the general contact details we actually want published, once those are
# settled on the contact and legal pages.
